Z||000000||Firebug||02-20-2001||08:05 PM||||When converting from a 4 cyl to a 2.8, do you need to get the steel hard lines from a 2.8 car from the fuel tank on, or are they the same?  <P>Thanks, <BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-20-2001||09:22 PM||||They should hook up at the same aprox. location. From the tank to rubber connecting lines to hard lines, through and beside (return line) fuel filter, to fitted (on ends) rubber lines to below the battery tray which connect to hard lines of engine. Just get the ones on the engine.||||reg||1
